mance-20261011.patch`).\n- typeError rows: strictness lives ONLY under `macro_probe_depth \u003e 0` (operators.rs `probe_abstract_*_error`, pattern_diagnostics.rs, macro_probe.rs) so ordinary compiles stay permissive.\n- Bare enum ctor names leaked from UNIMPORTED enums (`None`) — `visible_enum_variant` checks visibility.\n- `structural_call_type_arguments` dropped ALL type args when any arg was an anon — the synthesized PosInfos is one. Only args for generic formals count now.\n- TAST `Dynamic` args are usually DECAYED (erased generic returns, Array\u003cDynamic\u003e of raw ints): unboxing them for a scalar T lost 12 rows. Pre-existing T=Dynamic bugs filed fc36ea6.\n- Wait-loop trap: `until ssh nuc 'ps ... | grep gate'` matched its OWN command line; use `[g]ate` bracket patterns.\n- I ran `git stash` in ~/rz-bisect by accident once; `git stash pop` restored it. Check `git stash list` there if a build looks like HEAD.\n\n**2026-10-17: 1092/1092 (100%) at 0ab1a715 (pushed).** Coroutines on krio fibers (git-bug 8a3734f, closed) and eval.vm.Gc finalisation (approximate, c5ec0e4). Lessons:\n- HEISENBUGS that vanish when a trace is added = a REGISTER-KEYED set leaking across functions (`interface_wrapped_args` was never cleared; its stale entries had been hiding a double-wrap of abstract-over-interface args). Clear such sets where `boxed_value_regs` is cleared and save/restore them with lambda state.\n- Structural receivers go through the by-name stdlib class scan (stdlib_runtime.rs): needed for `{function pop():Int}` over arrays (Issue3071/2889); wrong for other typedef values (a3ed85e). Typedefs pre-registered as Class placeholders never upgrade (214f591); \"fixing\" that exposed the scan and lost TestMatch.\n- `return a; return b;` returned b until HIR blocks stopped at the first unconditional exit.\n- sync_nuc.sh now deletes files a patch creates first: an ignored leftover on the nuc made `git apply` fail and the build silently ran plain HEAD.\n\n---\nArchived from 